# Small-host systemd preset: the Rust shadow (prismd)

The shadow mirrors the TS verify profile's decisions without executing, so it is
the first thing to cap when RAM is tight: it costs ~10 MB and informs, it does
not trade.

Install:

```sh
sudo cp systemd/prismd-shadow.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now prismd-shadow.service
journalctl -u prismd-shadow.service -f
```

The profile path is positional (`ExecStart=.../prismd /root/.prismd/shadow.env`);
see `docs/plan/box-prismd-deploy.md` §7 for the env-mirror recipe that makes the
shadow read the SAME book as the profile it shadows.

[Unit]
Description=Prism shadow (prismd) — read-only decision mirror
After=network-online.target prism-profile@prism-paper-bin20.service
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
ExecStart=/root/.prismd/bin/prismd /root/.prismd/shadow.env
WorkingDirectory=/root/.prismd
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=60
MemoryMax=128M
MemoryHigh=96M
OOMPolicy=stop
CPUQuota=25%
LimitNOFILE=512
TasksMax=64
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=full
# The shadow must be able to READ the live book and write only its own state.
ReadOnlyPaths=/root/.local/share/prism
ReadWritePaths=/root/.prismd
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=prismd-shadow

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
